    "result": "I implemented `compare_versions` in `solution.py` and wrote a pytest suite in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 58 tests. The parser splits off `+BUILD` first, then `-PRERELEASE` at the first hyphen, and validates each part against the spec: no leading zeros in the core or numeric prerelease identifiers, no empty identifiers, and only ASCII letters, digits and `-`. Anything malformed raises `ValueError`. Precedence follows the spec: core numerically, a release beats a prerelease, prerelease identifiers compare numeric-vs-numeric, numeric below alphanumeric, ASCII string order, then fewer identifiers loses. Build metadata is ignored for ordering. The tests cover ordering, the spec's prerelease example chain, build-metadata equality, invalid inputs, and antisymmetry. I only edited `solution.py` and files under `tests/`, and used no other shell commands.",
